1sse|n|A round of business, amusement, or pleasure, daily or frequently pursued; especially, a course of business or offical duties regularly or frequently returning. ; Any regular course of action or procedure rigidly adhered to by the mere force of habit.	a:z2y,62,4~z2y,62,4	n:aex,53,3;16xg,40,2~aex,53,3;16xg,40,2	N:18lx,78,3~18lx,78,3
1sse|a|A round of business, amusement, or pleasure, daily or frequently pursued; especially, a course of business or offical duties regularly or frequently returning. ; Any regular course of action or procedure rigidly adhered to by the mere force of habit.	j:2bbb,17,3~2bbb,17,3
1sss|n|A noisy, turbulent quarrel or disturbance; a brawl. ; A series of persons or things arranged in a continued line; a line; a rank; a file; as, a row of trees; a row of houses or columns. ; The act of rowing; excursion in a rowboat.	a:24no,40,3;630,34,2;sli,32,5;1thb,21,2;1f87,9,2~sli,32,5;24no,40,3;630,34,2;1thb,21,2;1f87,9,2
